The model is persisted before the asynchronous credential write. If `providerKeys.set` rejects, the editor reports that saving failed and remains open, but the model has already been added. This creates a partial save and misleading retry behavior. The operations need rollback/transaction semantics or credential persistence must complete before committing the model.

